# ── Optional overrides only ──────────────────────────────────────────
# App defaults are hard-coded for Robinhood Chain testnet (46630):
#   Vault         0x7240…d740 @ block 126185021 (src/lib/config.ts TESTNET_POSEIDON_POOL)
#   GloamPayMemo  0x689e…5DCE @ block 90421567
#
# You do NOT need these on Vercel for testnet to work.
# Set only if you redeploy contracts or point at a fork.
# The mainnet pools are not env vars: they are filled in once, in
# src/lib/mainnet.ts (MAINNET_POOLS), and every mainnet stays hidden until then.
#
# DO NOT set NEXT_PUBLIC_POSEIDON_SHIELD_POOL to an earlier vault (0xA488…,
# 0xaEbB…, 0xAc25…, 0x4F38…12D8F): the app remaps those to the current vault
# automatically. Never point anything at 0x4F38…12D8F: that vault is drainable
# (audit H-P1).

# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSEIDON_SHIELD_POOL=0x72406D9597807A46f730d8b4fDBC5aC45Dc1d740
# NEXT_PUBLIC_HASH_SCHEME=poseidon
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHIELD_DEPLOY_BLOCK=126185021
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PAY_MEMO=0x689ebd9d30E0235c73fd8f10236F850CDB3c5DCE
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PAY_MEMO_DEPLOY_BLOCK=90421567

# Legacy keccak pool (no private trade):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_HASH_SCHEME=keccak
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHIELD_POOL_ADDRESS=0x2BD98196D90AB45D58843B4c8B8809aa34343d35

# ── Gloam wallets: Turnkey embedded wallets (email / passkey sign-in) ─
# Off unless all three are set. Dashboard steps, in order: DEPLOY-TURNKEY.md.
# All three are public (they ship in the browser bundle); none is a secret.
#   Organization ID      -> Turnkey dashboard, top-right account menu / Organization settings
#   Auth Proxy Config ID -> Embedded Wallets > Configuration (after enabling the auth proxy)
# Check the dashboard first (it must print no FAIL line):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNKEY_ORGANIZATION_ID=... NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNKEY_AUTH_PROXY_CONFIG_ID=... node scripts/turnkey-check.mjs
# Then the switch: exactly "true" turns sign-in on, on every network. Anything else is off.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNKEY_ORGANIZATION_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNKEY_AUTH_PROXY_CONFIG_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNKEY_ENABLED=true
#
# Optional: chains where Turnkey's gas station pays the network fee for a Gloam
# wallet that holds no gas, for adding money privately only (the vault deposit and
# the approve for it; never a public send or any other call). Needs Gas Sponsorship
# on in the dashboard, with spend limits; the
# fees are billed to the Turnkey account. Comma-separated chain ids, or "all".
# Unset = nothing sponsored: such a wallet then needs a little ETH. Tempo is never
# sponsored here (fees come out of the stablecoin). Suggested start, the L2s and testnets:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNKEY_SPONSOR_CHAINS=4663,8453,46630,84532,11155111
# Add 1 (Ethereum mainnet) only with a spend limit you are happy with: its fees are the highest.
#
# Optional: Continue with Google in the sign-in sheet. The Web client ID from Google
# Cloud (public, ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com; never the client secret). Unset,
# the button is not shown. Google must also be on in the Turnkey auth proxy config
# with the same client ID, and every origin listed in Google Cloud as both a JavaScript
# origin and a redirect URI (the origin itself, no path): DEPLOY-TURNKEY.md, "Continue with Google".
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNKEY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ── WalletConnect (wallet apps on phones, QR on desktop) ─────────────
# A public project id from dashboard.reown.com. Add gloam.trade, www.gloam.trade
# and localhost to the project's allowed domains. Unset = the option is hidden.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WC_PROJECT_ID=

# Optional: Discord/Slack/Make webhook for product events (server only)
# TRACTION_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/...

# ── Admin traction dashboard (/admin) ────────────────────────────────
# Required in production (server-only — never NEXT_PUBLIC_):
# ADMIN_ACCESS_CODE=long-random-secret
# Required locally too (app/.env.local): there is no built-in code.
# If cookies fail on a weird HTTPS setup: ADMIN_COOKIE_INSECURE=true
#
# Durable product-event store (recommended free Upstash Redis):
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://….upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=…
#
# People counts on /admin (server-only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_): 32 or more random
# characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. Each wallet that uses the app becomes
# HMAC-SHA256(this, address) and goes into Redis HyperLogLog counters, so no
# address is kept (lib/peopleStore). Keep it the same once set: a new value
# counts everyone again. Unset or shorter = nothing is counted.
# GLOAM_METRICS_SALT=

# ── Gloam relay (hides the sender's wallet on private sends + cash outs) ──
# Server-only key for a FRESH account that only pays gas. The same account
# relays on every network Gloam runs on: the testnets, and each mainnet once its
# pool is in (lib/mainnet.ts). It never holds user money (proofs authorize
# spends; cash-out recipients are bound inside the proof). Fund it per chain:
#   Tempo testnet:           PathUSD for fees (tempo_fundAddress faucet)
#   Robinhood Chain testnet: testnet ETH
#   Tempo mainnet:           real pathUSD for fees (or set the account's fee token to another USD stablecoin)
#   Robinhood Chain mainnet: real ETH
# Unset = relay off; the app falls back to "send from your wallet".
# GLOAM_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=
#
# Off unless exactly "on": the relay pays for a fresh wallet's Borro gas station
# on Robinhood Chain mainnet (make and pump only, /app/fresh-wallet). Limits are
# in src/lib/relay/gasStation.ts. The daily number is sends across everyone
# (default 40, under $1 of gas at today's prices).
# GLOAM_RELAY_GAS_STATION=on
# GLOAM_RELAY_GAS_STATION_DAILY=40
#
# Signs the memo ticket the relay hands back with each private send, so the
# payer's heads-up gets its own few relayed messages that strangers can't use
# up (payment commitments are public). Server only, 32+ random characters:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Unset (or shorter) = no tickets: every relayed message but a partner key's
# shares one small allowance per payment, which anyone can use up for a day.
# GLOAM_RELAY_MEMO_SECRET=
#
# Seals scheduled cash outs at rest (lib/relay/jobSeal): AES-256-GCM over each
# job's proof, public inputs and webhook, so reading Redis gives nobody a proof
# to send. Server only, 32 random bytes:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Unset or malformed = prepaid agent top-ups stay off, and cash outs in a window
# carry on stored in the clear as before. Keep a copy: without it sealed jobs
# can't send or be cancelled until it is back, or until 3 days past their send
# time, when the app moves their notes back. To rotate, put the new key here and
# the old one in
# GLOAM_RELAY_JOB_KEYS_OLD (comma separated). The cron re-seals what is waiting;
# keep the old key until gloam_cashout_later_resealed stops logging, plus 7 days.
# GLOAM_RELAY_JOB_KEY=
# GLOAM_RELAY_JOB_KEYS_OLD=

# ── Private RPC for the server (optional, recommended for launch traffic) ──
# Server reads and relay sends go out from Vercel's shared IPs, where a chain's
# public RPC starts answering 429 under load. Set a private endpoint per chain ID
# (server only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_); the public RPC stays behind it as a fallback.
# GLOAM_RPC_URL_4663=     # Robinhood Chain mainnet
# GLOAM_RPC_URL_4217=     # Tempo mainnet
# GLOAM_RPC_URL_8453=     # Base mainnet
# GLOAM_RPC_URL_1=        # Ethereum mainnet
# GLOAM_RPC_URL_99901=    # Elysium mainnet
# GLOAM_RPC_URL_46630=    # Robinhood Chain testnet
# GLOAM_RPC_URL_42431=    # Tempo testnet
# GLOAM_RPC_URL_84532=    # Base Sepolia
# GLOAM_RPC_URL_11155111= # Ethereum Sepolia

# ── Payment messages on Tempo (lets Gloam-address payees find payments) ──
# Live default: 0x3ca88712e9219b5EE4c82D31cAfEaB64C9E9b4E3 @ block 37410900.
# Override only if you redeploy it:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PAY_MEMO_TEMPO=0x...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PAY_MEMO_TEMPO_DEPLOY_BLOCK=

# ── Partner portal + Gloam API v1 (/partners, /api/v1) ──
# Server-only. Hashes API keys and signs partner sessions. At least 32 chars;
# never rotate it once keys exist (every issued key stops working).
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# GLOAM_API_KEY_PEPPER=
# Optional: a separate secret for partner sessions (defaults to one derived
# from the pepper). Rotating it signs every partner out.
# GLOAM_PARTNER_SESSION_SECRET=
# Optional: hosts a sign-in message may name (defaults to the request host).
# GLOAM_PARTNER_DOMAINS=gloam.trade,www.gloam.trade
# Partners and keys live in the Upstash Redis above. Local tests only:
# GLOAM_PARTNERS_STORE=memory

# Recording demo (?demo=1): on by default only on localhost. Set to 1 to allow it on a deployment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GLOAM_DEMO=1

# ── Testers program (/testers) ──
# The private Telegram group's join-request link. Shown only after someone
# applies, so the form stays the way in. Unset: applicants are told the invite
# comes on Telegram. Applications live in the Upstash Redis above.
# GLOAM_TESTERS_TELEGRAM_URL=https://t.me/+...
# Paid tester spots (default 31). Later applicants are kept as unpaid volunteers.
# GLOAM_TESTERS_CAP=31

# ── Telegram helper bot (/api/telegram, the t.me/gloamhq group) ──
# Server only. Setup steps are at the top of src/app/api/telegram/route.ts.
# Bot token from BotFather, and a long random secret Telegram sends back on
# every webhook call (A-Z, a-z, 0-9, _ and - only). Register the webhook with
#   TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=... TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=... node app/scripts/telegram-webhook.mjs
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Writes replies with the Anthropic API. Unset: the bot only sends its fixed replies.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults shown. claude-haiku-5-5 is the cheaper model.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# TELEGRAM_BOT_PERSONA=Glim
# Model calls per UTC day, for everyone together (defaults shown; 0 turns that
# kind off). Past a cap the bot sends only its fixed replies until the day turns.
# Also set a monthly spend limit in the Anthropic console.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_DAILY_ANSWERS=800
# TELEGRAM_BOT_DAILY_CHECKS=1500
# Replies in the owner's and admins' private chats with the bot, on their own cap.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_DAILY_DMS=200
# TELEGRAM_GROUP_ID=-1004464028206
# Admins, comma separated: the bot names them when something needs a person, and
# they can chat with it in private. Ids are safer (handles can change hands).
# TELEGRAM_ADMIN_HANDLES=
# TELEGRAM_ADMIN_IDS=
# Set to true when group testing starts; until then the bot says it starts soon.
# GLOAM_TESTING_OPEN=false
# In private the bot answers only the owner and the admins: both can chat with
# it, and the owner also gets reports (/report). Everyone else gets silence.
# Handles match without case; numeric owner ids win when set, since handles
# can change.
# TELEGRAM_OWNER_HANDLES=dukedotsol
# TELEGRAM_OWNER_IDS=
# Daily report to the owner at 21:00 WAT, sent by the Vercel cron in
# vercel.json. Off unless true; the owner must have messaged the bot once.
# Vercel sends CRON_SECRET as a Bearer token, so set it too.
# TELEGRAM_DAILY_REPORT=false
# CRON_SECRET=
# $GLOAM buy alerts: the helper posts every buy in the group's Buys topic, after
# each update and from the once-a-minute cron (/api/telegram/buys, needs
# CRON_SECRET). Optional: a USD floor, a different topic, or off with 0.
# TELEGRAM_BUY_MIN_USD=0
# TELEGRAM_BUYS_TOPIC=798
# TELEGRAM_BUY_ALERTS=1
# Memory, counters, welcomes and bug reports live in the Upstash Redis above.

# Bring money in from other chains (Relay, relay.link). Relay only delivers to
# mainnets, so the panel shows on mainnet networks. Set the preview flag to see
# it on testnet locally (it still bridges to mainnet).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BRIDGE_PREVIEW=1
# Relay API key, needed for Solana deposit addresses. Then also set:
# RELAY_API_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BRIDGE_SOLANA=1
# The id of that key, not the key itself (Relay Dashboard, under the app's API keys).
# /admin needs it to read Relay's full history: Relay's GET /requests/v3 hides keyed
# requests from a referrer filter without it, and the older v2 is retired on 24 Nov 2026.
# RELAY_API_KEY_ID=
# Optional Gloam fee on each bridge, in basis points (max 100), and where it goes.
# Both set: it comes out of each bridge and every quote shows it on its own line.
# BRIDGE_FEE_BPS=
# BRIDGE_FEE_RECIPIENT=0x...
